From b03d1df5b2a1713478481407bbaef13540a719c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:30:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keyboard layout key

Live = "Layout" shows the keyboard layout the helper reports
(/run/tiny-dfr/bridge/layout: the active number, then the short names) as
upper-case text. With Command = "Layout" a tap switches to the next layout
on release ("layout next" to the helper; without it the key's Action, for
example the layout toggle keys), and holding and sliding goes through the
layouts on the key itself, one per 90 px, picking one on release
("layout <n>"). The PNG preview shows a made-up layout.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
---
